WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.480
You spot

2
00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.740
AI art fast

3
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.520
because nothing

4
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.300
is wrong with it.

5
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.660
No smudges.

6
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.100
Your thumb keeps scrolling.

7
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.580
Yet an old Japanese

8
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.540
duplicator wins

9
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.220
by making small mistakes.

10
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.240
It's called a Risograph.

11
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.700
Riso Kagaku Corporation

12
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.320
built it

13
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.360
in the 1980s.

14
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.860
Thermal fiber stencils

15
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.280
push soy or rice-bran

16
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.300
ink through drums.

17
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.560
Each color takes

18
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.620
a separate pass.

19
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.860
So sheets shift slightly,

20
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.240
leaving misregistration

21
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.860
and halftone grain.

22
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.560
You end up looking twice.

23
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.880
Meanwhile, AI generators serve

24
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.160
airbrushed symmetry.

25
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.300
When curves are

26
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.220
scrubbed clean,

27
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.160
your brain detects

28
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.720
zero human agency.

29
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.120
Wabi-sabi

30
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.100
leans the other way.

31
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.700
An uneven ink edge

32
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:41.800
proves someone stood

33
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.560
at a press.

34
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.220
That gives it warmth.

35
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.060
You don't need

36
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.820
the hardware.

37
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.020
Drop paper tooth

38
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.920
and layer offsets

39
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.980
into digital work.

40
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.340
Smooth feeds blur together.

41
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.420
Let one plate

42
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.460
slip a hair,

43
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.240
and the piece

44
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.340
feels like yours.
